very annoying...any hack for this...? especially with copilot, effective context is 64k
- wondering if I can somehow override and "fool" opencode to think max model input-context is 2x -- i.e. 256k

EDIT:
I guess, I can do something like this, to artificially double max context?
```json
{
  "provider": {
    "openai": {
      "models": {
        "gpt-4o": {
          "limit": {
            "context": 131072,
            "output": 8192
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

should be fixed in next release if you set this in your opencode.json:
```
{
  "azure": {
      "env": [
        "AZURE_API"
      ],
      "models": {
        "gpt-5-codex": {
          "name": "GPT-5-codex",
          "options": {
            "parallelToolCalls": false, # or "store": false
          }
        }
      }
    }
}
```

